(*
  Run with:
    proverif -lib <hax>/hax-lib/proof-libs/proverif/primitives.pvl lib.pvl

  primitives.pvl ships with hax and declares the symbols this file
  uses but does not define: the public channel c, the construct_fail
  sink, bitstring_default and bitstring_err, the Some/None and
  True/False constructors, the nat_N literal constants, logical_and
  and logical_or, and the rust_primitives, core, and hax_lib opaque
  functions.

  A symbol this file uses that is defined neither here nor in
  primitives.pvl is listed in missingdecl.pvl, a diagnostic that is
  not part of the model. Define each such symbol — by hand or from
  another crate's extraction — or leave it abstract as an
  ideal-functionality boundary.
*)

